---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import data from '../data/banks.json';
import {savings} from '../lib/finance.mjs';
const illustration=(rate:number)=>savings({principal:10000,contribution:0,frequency:'monthly',annualRate:rate,years:1}).interest;
const dollars=(value:number)=>new Intl.NumberFormat('en-AU',{style:'currency',currency:'AUD'}).format(value);
const count=data.banks.reduce((sum,b)=>sum+b.productCount,0);
const date=new Date(data.fetchedAt).toLocaleDateString('en-AU',{timeZone:'Australia/Brisbane',day:'numeric',month:'long',year:'numeric'});
---
<Base title="Australian bank product explorer" description="Explore published Australian deposit product data. Find banks, inspect base rates and bonus conditions, and try a savings projection. Coverage and update dates disclosed.">
<header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Bank explorer</div><span class="hl-eyebrow">A MORE INFORMED SAVING MOVE</span><h1>Your bank.<br/>A little more context.</h1><p>Find a banking brand, inspect its published deposit products and take the numbers into your savings plan.</p></header>
<div class="hl-wrap hl-page-main"><div class="hl-bank-intro"><strong>{data.banks.length}</strong><div>banking brands in the public CDR register<br/>{count} deposit and transaction products retrieved · Snapshot {date}</div></div>
<p class="hl-help" style="max-width:800px;margin-bottom:22px">This directory covers banking brands in the CDR register, not every Australian bank or every product. Some providers have no deposit products, unavailable feeds or incomplete responses. Results are alphabetical, not a ranking. Eligibility, fees and product types vary; confirm them with the provider.</p>
<section class="hl-bank-reading"><h2>Read the account, not just the percentage.</h2><p>A useful comparison starts with the amount you will actually keep in an account, whether you can meet its conditions and what it costs. These listings are a starting point for your own checks.</p><ol><li><strong>Check access and eligibility.</strong> A transaction, restricted or offset account may not work like a general savings account.</li><li><strong>Separate the rate components.</strong> Base, bonus and introductory rates are different. Do not add them together unless the provider confirms that is how the offer works.</li><li><strong>Check time, balance caps and fees.</strong> A rate may apply only to part of a balance or only for a short period. A small fee can outweigh a modest rate increase.</li></ol>
<details class="hl-year-table"><summary>A worked comparison: when the higher rate leaves less money</summary><p>Two hypothetical accounts start with $10,000, no deposits or withdrawals and monthly compounding for one year. Account A pays 4.0% with no fee. Account B pays 4.6% with a $120 fee paid at the end of the year. These are teaching examples, not bank offers.</p><div class="hl-table-scroll"><table class="hl-table"><caption>One-year illustration before tax</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Account</th><th scope="col">Interest</th><th scope="col">Annual fee</th><th scope="col">Interest less fee</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">A · 4.0%</th><td>{dollars(illustration(4))}</td><td>$0.00</td><td>{dollars(illustration(4))}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">B · 4.6%</th><td>{dollars(illustration(4.6))}</td><td>$120.00</td><td>{dollars(illustration(4.6)-120)}</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Here, the higher-rate account leaves {dollars(illustration(4)-(illustration(4.6)-120))} less after the fee. Different balances, fee timing or bonus eligibility could change the comparison. Our savings calculator excludes fees, so compare costs separately.</p></details>
<p><a href="/learn/bonus-interest-conditions">Understand bonus rates and conditions →</a> · <a href="/methodology">How the data and calculations work →</a></p></section>
<label class="hl-field"><span>Find your bank or provider</span><input class="hl-search" type="search" id="bank-filter" placeholder="Try CommBank, ING, ANZ or Up…" aria-label="Find your bank or provider"/></label><p class="hl-help" id="bank-count" aria-live="polite">{data.banks.length} providers</p>
<div class="hl-bank-grid">{data.banks.map(b=><a class="hl-bank-row" data-bank-name={b.name.toLowerCase()} href={'/calculators/compound-interest?bank='+b.id}><span class="hl-bank-initial">{b.name.replace(/[^a-zA-Z]/g,'').slice(0,2).toUpperCase()}</span><div><h2>{b.name}</h2><small>{b.status==='unavailable'?'Data unavailable':b.productCount+' products'+(b.status==='partial'?' · partial data':'')}</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div>
<p id="bank-empty" class="hl-empty" hidden>No matching provider. You can still <a href="/calculators/compound-interest">enter your own interest rate</a>.</p>
<div class="hl-explainer"><div><h2>Public product data. No account access.</h2><p>We retrieve product information from the public APIs listed in the Australian Government’s Consumer Data Right register. These describe products and their terms; they contain no customer balances or transactions.</p><p>Snapshots show a retrieval date. The calculator can automatically model simple base variable rates and supported dollar-based tiers. It does not automatically combine bonus or introductory components or infer whether you qualify.</p></div><div><h2>Where the information comes from</h2><p><a href="https://www.cdr.gov.au/for-providers/how-find-data-holders-product-data-request-service">CDR: public product data ↗</a></p><p><a href="https://www.apra.gov.au/registers/list-registered-authorised-deposit-taking-institutions">APRA: authorised institutions ↗</a></p><p><a href="/methodology">Our coverage and rate methodology →</a></p></div></div></div>
</Base>
<script>
const input=document.querySelector('#bank-filter');const cards=[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-bank-name]')];
input?.addEventListener('input',()=>{const query=input.value.trim().toLowerCase();let count=0;cards.forEach(card=>{const show=card.dataset.bankName.includes(query);card.hidden=!show;if(show)count++;});document.querySelector('#bank-count').textContent=count+' matching providers';document.querySelector('#bank-empty').hidden=count!==0;});
</script>
